  "scientific_conclusion": [
    "Removing the structure-risk channel is not a common-domain repair. It strictly improves q99.999 error, maximum excess, and physical second-moment calibration in SIMBA and Swift, but slightly worsens all three in the TNG100 training domain.",
    "The no-risk candidate preserves high-k power and residual RMS in every domain and passes every field check in SIMBA and Swift. TNG100 fails only the frozen all-scale two-point-improvement check, so the mixed outcome is not explained by a wholesale loss of the stochastic field body.",
    "The V51 inference-only risk-zero improvement therefore does not transfer as a universal causal effect under matched retraining. Risk is a domain-dependent amplifier or proxy whose utility interacts with the remaining backbone conditioning.",
    "No new model is selected from this mixed result. The frozen next step is a read-only V52-versus-V50 audit of domainwise extreme errors, the failed TNG100 two-point scales, and high-backbone strata before any architecture, loss, feature, or threshold change."
